# Build and harness

Read `AGENTS.md` plus the target runbook ([[runbook — Stellar]] / [[runbook — Marlowe]]) before changing build or submit paths.

## Makefile / harness flags

- Document flag changes in commit messages and session handoff.
- Harness vars (`GPU_MHD`, `GPU_GRAV`, `GPU_NPRE`, `GPU_FASTMATH`, `CUB_SORT_*`) map to Makefile `MHD`, `GRAV`, `NPRE`, `FASTMATH`, etc.
- GPU builds on cluster: **serial `make` only** (no `-j`).
- Stellar `Makefile.a100`: default `NPRE=4`, `CUDA_ARCH=sm_80`.
- Marlowe `Makefile.h100`: default `NPRE=8`, `CUDA_ARCH=sm_90`.
- Cross-check Stellar vs Marlowe drift before copying namelists or plot commands.

## Profiling and debug

- Never enable `DEBUG=1` for performance benchmarks without noting it in handoff / run-log.
- NCU/Nsys cases: cite exact `./submit_profiles.sh` case name (e.g. `nsys-l7`, `ncu-ot`, `ot-amr`).

## Submit suggestions

When proposing a run, include:

1. Harness directory (`~/hackathon` or `~/marlowe/hackathon`)
2. Full command with case name and relevant env overrides
3. Expected binary (`ramses3d`, `ramses3d.mhd`, `ramses3d.hydro`)
4. Sanity checks in `run.log`

## Namelists

- Show diff for any default change.
- Warn about 80-char path truncation; prefer staged `ic_grafic` symlink over long absolute paths.
